# calendar.dat - when contests run (#4, item 3)
#
# RULES, NOT DATES. Contest schedules recur by rule - "the second full
# weekend of August" - so that is what ships, and the dates are computed for
# whatever year is asked about. A bundled list of 2026 dates would be
# silently stale in 2027, and the box that most needs to know what is on is
# often the one at a field site with no way to refresh it.
#
# Format, one record per line, pipe-separated:
#   ContestId|Name|Rule|Month|Nth|DurationDays|FixedDay
#
# ContestId     joins to contests.dat; may be empty for an event we can date
#               but have no exchange definition for
# Name          human-readable
# Rule          NTH_WEEKEND | LAST_WEEKEND | NTH_SATURDAY | FIXED
# Month         1-12
# Nth           1-5 for NTH_* rules; ignored by LAST_WEEKEND and FIXED
# DurationDays  days the event covers - 2 for a weekend, 1 for a single day
# FixedDay      day of month, FIXED only; 0 otherwise
#
# An unrecognised rule REJECTS the row rather than being approximated:
# guessing at a recurrence would put the event in the wrong weekend and look
# authoritative doing it.
#
# -- PROVENANCE ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# These recurrence rules are UNCONFIRMED, in the same sense as contests.dat:
# they were written from general knowledge of when these parties run, not
# from each sponsor's published schedule. Sponsors do move events between
# years.
#
# The consequence is bounded and worth stating plainly: a wrong rule here
# shows the operator the wrong weekend. That is annoying but visible - unlike
# a wrong EXCHANGE, which would corrupt a submitted log - which is why this
# file does not carry a machine-readable CONFIRMED column the way
# contests.dat does. Treat every date below as a prompt to check, not as an
# authority.
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.
#
MDC-QSO-PARTY|Maryland-DC QSO Party|NTH_WEEKEND|8|2|2|0
CQP|California QSO Party|NTH_WEEKEND|10|1|2|0
PAQP|Pennsylvania QSO Party|NTH_WEEKEND|10|2|2|0
OHQP|Ohio QSO Party|LAST_WEEKEND|8|0|1|0
TXQP|Texas QSO Party|LAST_WEEKEND|9|0|2|0
FLQP|Florida QSO Party|NTH_WEEKEND|4|4|2|0
